    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so if it's yellowing, is that definitely a nitrogen problem or could it be something else? like how can i tell if it's actually lacking phosphorus specifically? i noticed some weird purple-ish tints in some spots too.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing can be caused by various issues, such as poor watering or soil compaction, so it might not solely be a nitrogen deficiency. Purple tints are often a sign of phosphorus deficiency, though some other soil conditions can also cause discoloration. To diagnose, check your soil and ensure proper watering before blindly applying fertilizer. If you suspect phosphorus, a granular fertilizer with a higher middle number, like a 10-20-10, might be appropriate.",
      "source": "target",
